MAC_NONE(4)              BSD Kernel Interfaces Manual              MAC_NONE(4)

NNAAMMEE
     mmaacc__nnoonnee — null MAC policy module

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile the null policy into your kernel, place the following lines in
     your kernel configuration file:

           ooppttiioonnss MMAACC
           ooppttiioonnss MMAACC__NNOONNEE

     Alternately, to load the none module at boot time, place the following
     line in your kernel configuration file:

           ooppttiioonnss MMAACC

     and in loader.conf(5):

           mac_none_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmaacc__nnoonnee policy module implements a none MAC policy that has no ef‐
     fect on access control in the system.  Unlike mac_stub(4), none of the
     MAC entry points are defined.

   LLaabbeell FFoorrmmaatt
     No labels are defined for mmaacc__nnoonnee.

